A||||5||Harry||Factory Octane ratings?
Z||000000||Harry||08-09-99||08:40 PM||||What was the original factory rating for recommended fuels for the 85 GT 2.8<br>I have not bought the manual yet&gt;
Z||000001||Cooter||08-09-99||10:26 PM||||I would say just run what the car will tolerate. If it runs on 87 with no problems then run it. My 85 4cyl spark knocks really bad with anything less than 93 octane while my civic will run fine on the cheapest stuff I can find. I guess that I could back the timing off a little, but that would require a little effort. . 
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-10-99||06:52 AM||||Yeah, what's the deal with Dukes and premium gas?  Both Dukes I've owned pinged like crazy with anything less than 92 octane, yet my V6 SE runs happily on 89 and only pings slightly on 87.  What gives?  
Z||000003||Harry||08-10-99||06:23 PM||||Well i've run as low as 87 with no pings in mine.<br>However the other day was extremely hot here.<br>I ran a full tank of Prem system 3 and the engine temp was running about 200 @ steady 70 mph speeds for about 2 hours and the car ran much smoother than normal ( you could just feel it if you know what I mean ) I wasnt sure whether the weather did it or the change in mo-jo.<br>I had ran it before but never really on a long trip so it may not have been apparent.
Z||000004||theogre||08-11-99||08:03 AM||||I had allot of ping in my 87 4 cyl, even with premium gas. Then I locked the fan on so it wouldn't heat up in slow traffic. that helped allot. (we get allot of slow traffic here....... ) In slow traffic the ECM would report the block at around 220-225, if not more. With the fan on it never goes above 210-215 with a 195 stat in it. pretty much all the ping went away.<p>Then try a 180F thermostat in your 4 cyl. It'll drop the temp to about 190F in the block. It's cheap. The 87 likes it allot, I don't know how much the pre 87s will like it since they are set up so diferant, but it can't hurt. I seem to be getting a slight boost in performance, but mostly the thing just seems to run better. It never pings now, even on 100F days.
Z||000005||theogre||08-12-99||02:46 PM||||btw.... I put a tank of 89 octain gas in it, been a couple days now, it's fairly warm out... even climbing it's not pinging with it's current setup. performance with the cheeper gas is the same.
